## Data Selection at Scale

Exercises the per-datum styling pipeline when `selection.enabled` is on across every series type that supports data selection. Two scenarios per series: zoom with no selection (cold path) and zoom with ~50% of datums selected (warm path). Each series family runs as a separate example to keep a benchmark run within a single page session's memory budget.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Data Selection Zoom (Line / Area)" name="data-selection-zoom-line-area" type="generated" initialLoadDeferred=true /%}

{% chartExampleRunner title="Data Selection Zoom (Bar)" name="data-selection-zoom-bar" type="generated" initialLoadDeferred=true /%}

{% chartExampleRunner title="Data Selection Zoom (Financial)" name="data-selection-zoom-financial" type="generated" initialLoadDeferred=true /%}

{% chartExampleRunner title="Data Selection Zoom (Scatter / Bubble / Histogram)" name="data-selection-zoom-xy" type="generated" initialLoadDeferred=true /%}

## Series Label Collision

Exercises the cross-series label placement pass: clustered bubble labels that cascade through their fallback placements, and bar labels that cascade and shrink. Each series runs with labels off, at a single placement, and with the full cascade, so the cost of placement is separated from the cost of drawing the labels. The highlight case measures the cached-solve path a hover takes.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Series Label Collision" name="series-labels-collision" type="generated" initialLoadDeferred=true /%}

